0..78 Comment "/// This source states maps out of the spheres by cases, and `Path.ap` of them"
79..105 Comment "/// on the spheres\' cells."
106..109 Comment "///"
110..184 Comment "/// A case over a sphere takes an arm at the point and an arm at the cell."
185..262 Comment "/// The arm at the cell is a cell of the answer at the reflexivity of the arm"
263..280 Comment "/// at the point."
281..359 Comment "/// `Path.ap f surf` acts on the 2-cell as the action of `Path.ap f` on paths."
360..436 Comment "/// It takes one layer per reflexivity between the cell\'s type and the map\'s"
437..448 Comment "/// domain."
449..524 Comment "/// It reduces to the case\'s arm at the cell, by the rule at dimension one."
525..528 Comment "///"
529..604 Comment "/// The checker converts each image to the arm, and the kernel replays each"
605..680 Comment "/// reduction. A dependent case into a path family owes no arm at the cell."
681..748 Comment "/// The family at the cell carries the answer along the bound path."
749..817 Comment "/// Transport along the cell reads that endpoint by the family\'s two"
818..895 Comment "/// endpoints, one `Path.ap` layer deeper. The checker converts the transport"
896..972 Comment "/// of the answer to the answer, and the kernel re-derives the same reading."
973..976 Comment "///"
977..1055 Comment "/// Limits: the rule reads a path family alone. It reduces the transport where"
1056..1132 Comment "/// the answer at the point is reflexivity, or where both images of the cell"
1133..1205 Comment "/// are empty (`sphere-whiskers.gandr`). An arm written at the cell of a"
1206..1283 Comment "/// dependent case is checked at the motive\'s own type, so it does not check."
1284..1287 Comment "///"
1288..1349 Comment "/// - see: #6458 — `selfrefl2`, `throughName2`, `selfrefl3`"
1350..1429 Comment "/// - see: corpus/pathological/identity/sphere-maps.gandr — a map with no arm"
1430..1471 Comment "///   at the cell, which the case refuses"
1472..1506 Comment "/// - see: #6477 — `apEmptyCell`"
1507..1571 Comment "/// - see: #6531 — the answer at the point that holds a letter"
1572..1626 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere-whiskers.gandr"
1627..1672 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere.gandr"
1673..1723 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/circle-maps.gandr"
1724..1767 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/hopf.gandr"
